      },
      "message": "fix(app): judge a tap's cutting moves at its thread's core in the op verify\n\nA tap on a hole modelled at tap-drill size was still refused after the\nprogram sim learned to sweep its core (#713): the generator's own verify\nread the full major diameter against the hole wall and convicted the feed\nin and out as gouges. Generate now re-runs the cutting laws with the tap\ncut to its ISO 724 basic minor diameter and drops each Gouge the core run\ndoes not also raise. Rapids, shank, holder and fixture verdicts keep the\nfull diameter; a hole under the minor diameter, a tap over solid metal or\ndeeper than its hole is still convicted. Builds on austin62jake's\ncutting_radius and tap_sim fixtures from #271/#713.\n\nFixes #266\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
