      },
      "message": "fix(app): keep a tap's shank verdict when its core re-read drops the gouge\n\nThe solid law reports a move once (Gouge, else the body), so the\nfull-diameter Gouge hid a shank collision the core run did see: an M6\ntap with a Ø6 shank and 4 mm thread length fed 12 mm into a Ø5 hole\nposted with no warning. For every move whose Gouge is dropped, carry\nthe core run's ShankHit/SweepHit/HolderHit/FixtureHit on that move.\nThe re-read is also limited to the tapping cycles (Tap, FloatingTap,\nAuto). Two pins now assert the Gouge itself, not any warning.\n\nPinned by a_tap_whose_shank_rides_into_the_hole_is_still_convicted.\n\nRefs #266\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
